### Well done on this test file

### GET a specific book
GET http://localhost:3000/api/books/6a2a35d9d859a9ad271b25d2
content-type: application/json

### GET all books
GET http://localhost:3000/api/books
content-type: application/json

### Create a book
POST http://localhost:3000/api/books
content-type: application/json

{
    "title": "Sample",
    "author": "Jhon Doe",
    "pages": 200
}

### Patch a book
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/books/6a2a35d9d859a9ad271b25d2
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "title": "updated title"
}


### DELETE a book (also cascade-deletes its notes)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/books/6a2a359dd859a9ad271b25d1
Content-Type: application/json


### GET all notes for a book
GET http://localhost:3000/api/books/6a2a35d9d859a9ad271b25d2/notes
content-type: application/json

### Create a note for a book
POST http://localhost:3000/api/books/6a2a35d9d859a9ad271b25d2/notes
content-type: application/json

{
    "content": "Great chapter on closures.",
    "page": 42
}

### Create a note with empty content (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/api/books/6a2a35d9d859a9ad271b25d2/notes
content-type: application/json

{
    "content": "   "
}

### Patch a note
PATCH http://localhost:3000/api/notes/6a2a35d9d859a9ad271b25e9
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "content": "Updated note text",
    "page": 50
}

### DELETE a note
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/notes/6a2a35d9d859a9ad271b25e9
Content-Type: application/json
